### One datastore name, several clusters

Every HVM cluster has datastores of its own — `local`, `morpheus-cloud-init`,
`morpheus-images` — so on an appliance with more than one cluster a lookup by `name`
alone finds one per cluster and fails. Set `cluster_id` to look the name up among
that cluster's datastores only (`GET /api/clusters/{id}/datastores`); with `id`, the
datastore must be one the cluster has. `cluster_id` is a filter on the lookup rather
than a property of the datastore, so it is carried through as configured and never
read back.

